  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nA non-VAT-registered seller cannot issue a VAT invoice. Under Section 236 of the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC), only VAT-registered persons are authorized to issue VAT invoices. A VAT invoice is a specific document that must be issued by sellers who are registered for VAT, reflecting the VAT charged on sales of goods or services.\n\nFurthermore, Revenue Regulation No. 16-2005 clarifies that a \"VAT-registered person\" is defined as someone who is registered as a VAT taxpayer under Section 236 of the NIRC. Therefore, if a seller is not registered for VAT, they are not permitted to issue VAT invoices, as doing so would misrepresent their tax status and could lead to penalties.\n\nIn summary, the legal basis for this position is found in:\n1. **NIRC Section 236** - Registration requirements for VAT.\n2. **RR 16-2005** - Definitions and regulations regarding VAT-registered persons and invoicing.\n\n### Relevant Facts / Assumptions\nThe factual circumstances have not been fully described. The analysis is based on the question as presented.\n\n### Alternative Interpretations\nNo alternative interpretations identified from the available indexed authorities.\n\n### Position Strength\nPosition strength is preliminary and subject to full fact pattern verification.",
